  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc. The key open question is whether adding the image modality via fusion can push beyond this strong RNA-only baseline. Config_032 directly extends config_006 by adding resnet50 image features with concat fusion, keeping all other settings identical (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer). This isolates the effect of multimodal fusion. Using resnet50 (already tested at 0.208 image-only) means we know the image signal is weak, making this a conservative, clean test: if even the simplest fusion of a weak image signal doesn't beat 0.653, it strongly argues against pursuing multimodal further and lets us redirect remaining budget to RNA-only refinements. If it does help, we have 3 experiments left to try ViT-L or weighted fusion. This is the highest-information single experiment given the budget."
}

